# The web intake process's broker login (docs 04, 05). Copy to .env.intake.mqtt, which is gitignored; never commit a real
# password. Same shape as .env.mqtt (the bridge's login), and the same rule: this file holds ONLY the two keys below, and
# intake/intake_mqtt.py refuses any other key (the Gemini key lives in .env.intake, never here).
#
# web-intake is a broker user whose ACL allows exactly one thing: writing force/telemetry/web-intake (infra/mosquitto/acl). Its password
# is set where the others are (doc 05, "The broker on the desktop"), and each credential has one home: this one is here.
# Values already in the process environment win over this file.
INTAKE_MQTT_USERNAME=web-intake
INTAKE_MQTT_PASSWORD=
